invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: sha512_hw.c passes a round's words plus their constants through
  veor3q_u64, one of FEAT_SHA3's four instructions, which the file's
  target attribute turns on beside FEAT_SHA512's. The other two operands
  are one vector read twice through its volatile pointer, so neither
  compiler removes the exclusive ORs, the value is the same, every digest
  is right and no vector or equivalence case sees the edit. A session
  whose caller stated CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512 then runs an
  instruction that bit does not name, on a statement about its timing
  nobody made (docs/decisions.md 93). The script compiles the file for
  arm64 under the pinned clang and requires none of the four in its
  object.

--- old
    c->with_constants = vaddq_u64(current, vld1q_u64(&K[2 * pair]));
--- new
    c->with_constants = veor3q_u64(vaddq_u64(current, vld1q_u64(&K[2 * pair])), kept(&c->ab_start),
                                   kept(&c->ab_start));
